The profile pod is the only one whose restart count climbs, and it has no spans after 12:20:10. The evidence is consistent, so I'm writing up the answer.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "profile",
      "fault_kind": "pod_unavailable",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT 'norm' p, max(time) last_t, min(time) first_t FROM normal_traces WHERE service_name='profile' UNION ALL SELECT 'abn', max(time), min(time) FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='profile'", "claim": "profile emits spans in the normal period up to 12:20:10 and none at all in the abnormal window."},
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT attr_k8s_pod_name pod, min(value) vmin, max(value) vmax, min(time) t0, max(time) t1, count(*) n FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE metric='k8s.container.restarts' GROUP BY 1 HAVING max(value)>min(value) ORDER BY 1", "claim": "The profile pod's restart count climbs from 2 to 6 during the abnormal window; no other pod restarts."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_status_code st, count(*) n, approx_quantile(duration,0.5)/1e6 p50ms, min(time) t0, max(time) t1 FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='frontend' AND span_name LIKE 'profile.Profile/%' GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "frontend's GetProfiles calls to profile all fail with Error in about 0.01 ms from 12:20:14 onward."},
        {"kind": "log", "sql": "SELECT service_name, level, message, count(*) n FROM abnormal_logs WHERE level='ERROR' GROUP BY 1,2,3", "claim": "frontend logs 1155 ERROR entries 'Get profiles failed' between 12:20:14 and 12:25:13."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {"from": "profile", "to": "frontend",
     "evidence": [
       {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_status_code st, attr_http_response_status_code code, count(*) n FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='frontend' AND span_name='HTTP /recommendations' GROUP BY 1,2,3", "claim": "frontend's HTTP /recommendations server spans return 500 Error for 851 of 854 requests after profile goes silent."}
     ]}
  ]
}
```

